HTML entry point support and add configuration details for webpack 5.108.0\n\n* docs(optimization): add explanation and examples for cross-module dead-branch skipping in inlining\n\n* docs(target): add support for Bun and Deno targets in webpack 5.108.0\n\n* docs(module): update localIdentName description to include new hash options in webpack 5.108.0\n\n* docs(output): add logical assignment support and HTML file generation options in webpack 5.108.0\n\n* docs(api): add description of the platform property on Compiler instance in webpack 5.108.0\n\n* docs(module): add css-url option to extract url() references in CSS attributes in webpack 5.108.0\n\n* blog: webpack 5.108 (#8277)\n\n* blog: webpack 5.108\n\n* docs: add sections for HTML output from JavaScript entries and automatic ES module detection\n\n* docs: clarify ES module detection in configuration examples\n\n* docs: enhance description of Webpack 5.108 features and clarify the `universal` target\n\n* docs: improve clarity and formatting in Webpack 5.108 blog post\n\n* docs: add Bun and Deno targets section to Webpack 5.108 blog post\n\n* docs: add Open Graph image for Webpack 5.108 blog post\n\n* docs: add detection information for universal builds in Webpack 5.108 blog post\n\n* update date\n\n* docs: document webpack 5.107/5.108 CLI config formats and HTML module extraction (#8284)\n\n* docs(cli): document JSON5, YAML and TOML config file support\n\nCover the webpack-cli 7.1.0 ability to load static configuration from\n.json5, .yaml/.yml and .toml files, including the on-demand parser\npackages, and note the supported extensions in the default config lookup.\n\n* docs(cli): use double quotes in JSON5 config example for prettier\n\n* docs(configuration): document HTML module extraction options\n\nAdd module.generator.html.extract and the matching output.htmlFilename /\noutput.htmlChunkFilename templates introduced in webpack 5.107.0 for the\nexperimental HTML module pipeline.\n\n* docs: simplify config-language wording, drop interpret and peerDependencies jargon\n\n* fix: handle null OpenCollective accounts (#8292)\n\n* docs: document `progressBar` option of `ProgressPlugin` (#8289)\n\nCo-authored-by: Sebastian Beltran <bjohansebas@gmail.com>\n\n* docs: update webpack-dev-server API documentation for version 6 (#8290)\n\n* chore(deps): bump cypress-io/github-action (#8285)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 1 update in the / directory: [cypress-io/github-action](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action).\n\n\nUpdates `cypress-io/github-action` from 7.4.0 to 7.4.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/compare/948d67d3074f1bbb6379c8bdbb04e95d2f8e593f...fa4a118725a8f001170d49631ea89e5d66fee626)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: cypress-io/github-action\n  dependency-version: 7.4.1\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(native-css): expand CSS migration guide off css-loader/style-loader/mini-css-extract-plugin (#8294)\n\n* docs(native-css): expand CSS migration guide\n\nAdd a full migration path off css-loader, style-loader, and\nmini-css-extract-plugin: module-type and exportType overviews,\nper-loader option mapping tables, a complete native parser/generator\noption reference with defaults, and popular recipes.\n\n* docs(native-css): cover SSR sync, getJSON, and more CSS Modules features\n\nReframe getLocalIdent/getJSON as achievable (localIdentName function form\nand module-graph exports) rather than unsupported, add a Server-side\nrendering section showing deterministic localIdentName across node/web\ntargets, document supported CSS Modules features (composes, @value,\n:export, :local/:global), and add a webpackIgnore tip.\n\n* docs(native-css): fix eslint errors in code blocks\n\nWrap the css-loader before-example in a full config so it parses as a\nmodule instead of a bare object literal, and alphabetize the named\nimports in the CSS Modules example to satisfy import/order.\n\n* test(e2e): wait for service worker before going offline\n\nThe offline spec cut the network immediately after the first visit, while\nthe service worker was still precaching the site in its install handler.\nGoing offline aborts that precache, so the worker never activates and the\nnext navigation times out waiting for a load event. Wait for an activated\nregistration before going offline so the precache is guaranteed complete.\n\n* test(e2e): await serviceWorker.ready with a 60s timeout\n\nThe previous wait asserted on getRegistration().active, but the retry\nbudget was the default 4s (the timeout on cy.window does not propagate to\nthe chained .should), so it gave up while the worker was still precaching\nand failed with \"active service worker: expected undefined to exist\".\nAwait navigator.serviceWorker.ready — which resolves only once an\nactivated worker exists — with an explicit 60s command timeout.\n\n* test(e2e): put the 60s SW-ready timeout on .invoke, not .then\n\nThe two-arg cy.window().then(options, cb) form tripped\nunicorn/catch-error-name (it reads the callback as a promise rejection\nhandler). Poll getRegistration() and carry the 60s budget on .invoke,\nwhich the chained .should inherits — no two-arg .then, lint-clean, and\nstill waits for the worker to activate before going offline.\n\n* fix(sw): make precache install non-atomic\n\ncache.addAll precaches the whole manifest atomically, so a single failed\nrequest (e.g. a connection dropped while fetching the entire manifest at\nonce) rejects the install and the worker never activates — breaking\noffline support entirely. Precache each entry independently and tolerate\nper-entry failures; uncached entries fall back to the network. This also\nfixes the flaky offline E2E spec, which timed out waiting for a worker\nthat never activated.\n\n* fix(sw): precache in bounded batches so install can''t stall\n\nNon-atomic precache still fired a request for every manifest entry at\nonce. Flooding the network that way can leave some requests unsettled, so\nthe install''s waitUntil never resolves and the worker never activates —\noffline stays broken (and the offline E2E spec times out waiting for an\nactive worker). Precache in bounded batches of 10 so install completes\nreliably and the worker activates promptly.\n\n* Revert speculative service-worker and offline-test changes\n\nThe offline E2E failure is that the service worker never reaches the\nactive state within 60s in CI — reproduced identically with the original\natomic precache, a non-atomic variant, and bounded batches, so the\nprecache strategy is not the cause. Revert those unproven production/test\nchanges; the guide change alone remains.\n\n* test(e2e): temporary SW-state diagnostic for offline spec\n\nEncode the service worker registration state (installing/waiting/active)\ninto the assertion message so the CI log reveals why the worker never\nreaches the active state. To be reverted once diagnosed.\n\n* test(e2e): await serviceWorker.ready before going offline\n\nThe diagnostic run showed the registration exists but its\ninstalling/waiting/active worker properties read as undefined in Cypress''\ncross-realm context, so polling registration.active can never observe the\nworker even once it activates. Await navigator.serviceWorker.ready\ninstead — the browser resolves it internally when an activated worker\ncontrols the scope — giving the worker time to precache and activate\nbefore the test cuts the network.\n\n* Add atproto-did file with DID entry (#8295)\n\n* chore(deps): bump websocket-driver from 0.7.4 to 0.7.5 (#8298)\n\nBumps [websocket-driver](https://github.com/faye/websocket-driver-node) from 0.7.4 to 0.7.5.\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/faye/websocket-driver-node/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/faye/websocket-driver-node/compare/0.7.4...0.7.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: websocket-driver\n  dependency-version: 0.7.5\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump ws (#8299)\n\nBumps  and [ws](https://github.com/websockets/ws). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `ws` from 8.20.1 to 8.21.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/websockets/ws/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/websockets/ws/compare/8.20.1...8.21.1)\n\nUpdates `ws` from 7.5.10 to 7.5.12\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/websockets/ws/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/websockets/ws/compare/8.20.1...8.21.1)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: ws\n  dependency-version: 8.21.1\n  dependency-type: indirect\n- dependency-name: ws\n  dependency-version: 7.5.12\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump systeminformation from 5.31.6 to 5.31.17 (#8301)\n\nBumps [systeminformation](https://github.com/sebhildebrandt/systeminformation) from 5.31.6 to 5.31.17.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/sebhildebrandt/systeminformation/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/sebhildebrandt/systeminformation/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/sebhildebrandt/systeminformation/compare/v5.31.6...v5.31.17)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: systeminformation\n  dependency-version: 5.31.17\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@