ck 5.109\n\n* feat: add output.html options for script loading, title, meta tags, base element, and resource hints in webpack 5.109\n\n* docs: clarify deprecation notice for import.meta.webpackContext in module documentation for webpack 5.109\n\n* feat: add blog post for Webpack 5.109 release highlighting new features and improvements\n\n* Update changes\n\n* chore: renderatl (#8317)\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump postcss and @tailwindcss/postcss (#8318)\n\nBumps [postcss](https://github.com/postcss/postcss) and [@tailwindcss/postcss](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/tree/HEAD/packages/@tailwindcss-postcss). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `postcss` from 8.5.15 to 8.5.25\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/compare/8.5.15...8.5.25)\n\nUpdates `@tailwindcss/postcss` from 4.3.1 to 4.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/tailwindlabs/tailwindcss/commits/v4.3.3/packages/@tailwindcss-postcss)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: postcss\n  dependency-version: 8.5.25\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n- dependency-name: \"@tailwindcss/postcss\"\n  dependency-version: 4.3.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps-dev): bump fast-uri from 3.1.4 to 3.1.5 (#8320)\n\nBumps [fast-uri](https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri) from 3.1.4 to 3.1.5.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/compare/v3.1.4...v3.1.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: fast-uri\n  dependency-version: 3.1.5\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Fix: side bar overflowing (#8322)\n\nSigned-off-by: Pranav-IIITM <jogdandpranav2007@gmail.com>\n\n* docs(plugin): add testing guidance for plugin authors (#8312)\n\n* docs(plugin): add testing guidance for plugin authors\n\n* docs: fix plugin testing markdown formatting\n\n* Update changes\n\n* docs: remove render banners (#8329)\n\n* docs: remove render banners\n\n* chore: remove render atl references\n\n* Comment out copy CNAME\n\n* chore(deps): bump the dependencies group across 1 directory with 2 updates (#8333)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 2 updates in the / directory: [errata-ai/vale-action](https://github.com/errata-ai/vale-action) and [cypress-io/github-action](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action).\n\n\nUpdates `errata-ai/vale-action` from 2.1.2 to 3.0.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/errata-ai/vale-action/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/errata-ai/vale-action/compare/85f9f7f2c5f449ac0ae5b66662961bae3f77ca6a...518a9136acc6e6668ce7c00d367051e0941e87ff)\n\nUpdates `cypress-io/github-action` from 7.4.1 to 7.4.2\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/compare/fa4a118725a8f001170d49631ea89e5d66fee626...c32f12761482a282d24ca0fd7466d8ae86f54ba8)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: errata-ai/vale-action\n  dependency-version: 3.0.0\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-major\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: cypress-io/github-action\n  dependency-version: 7.4.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add automated migration guidance for native CSS (#8334)\n\n* docs: clarify splitChunks request defaults (#8332)\n\n* chore(deps): bump brace-expansion (#8335)\n\nBumps  and [brace-expansion](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion). These dependencies needed to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `brace-expansion` from 1.1.14 to 1.1.18\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/compare/v1.1.14...v1.1.18)\n\nUpdates `brace-expansion` from 5.0.6 to 5.0.9\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/compare/v1.1.14...v1.1.18)\n\nUpdates `brace-expansion` from 2.1.0 to 2.1.4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/compare/v1.1.14...v1.1.18)\n\nUpdates `brace-expansion` from 2.1.1 to 2.1.4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/juliangruber/brace-expansion/compare/v1.1.14...v1.1.18)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: brace-expansion\n  dependency-version: 1.1.18\n  dependency-type: indirect\n- dependency-name: brace-expansion\n  dependency-version: 5.0.9\n  dependency-type: indirect\n- dependency-name: brace-expansion\n  dependency-version: 2.1.4\n  dependency-type: indirect\n- dependency-name: brace-expansion\n  dependency-version: 2.1.4\n  dependency-type: indirect\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump cypress-io/github-action in the dependencies group (#8336)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 1 update: [cypress-io/github-action](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action).\n\n\nUpdates `cypress-io/github-action` from 7.4.2 to 7.4.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/compare/c32f12761482a282d24ca0fd7466d8ae86f54ba8...09090944bd8aaa2a517cefb6e38bf1aae336b42b)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: cypress-io/github-action\n  dependency-version: 7.4.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update changes\n\n* docs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage (#8339)\n\n* docs: native HTML guide and expanded native CSS coverage\n\nAdd a Native HTML guide covering the built-in HTML support: HTML entry\npoints, generated pages, HTML imported from JS, the parser''s source list,\ntemplating, minification, resource hints, HMR and plugin hooks, plus\nmigration paths off html-loader and html-webpack-plugin.\n\nExpand the Native CSS guide with @custom-media / @custom-selector, the\nbuilt-in CSS minimizer (including browserslist vendor prefixing), font\npreloading and url hints, CSS referenced from HTML, and more examples.\n\nDocument optimization.minimize''s per-asset-type object form and the entry\ndescriptor html option, which both guides reference.\n\n* docs: complete HTML parser, generator and output option reference\n\nAdd an \"All options with examples\" section to the Native HTML guide\ncovering every option: the html parser (sources with all source types,\nas, urlHints, template), the generator (extract), output.html and the\nhtml filename templates, output.resourceHints with its hint and url-rule\ndescriptors, every optimization.minimize.html transform, and the HTML\nmagic comments.\n\n* docs: use built-in CSS in examples, deprecate the superseded loaders/plugins\n\nMark style-loader, css-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin as deprecated on the loaders and plugins index pages,\neach pointing at the native support guide.\n\nReplace the CSS-loader examples with the built-in support: asset\nmanagement (no install, no rule, extracted stylesheet — transcripts\nregenerated from real builds), advanced entry, concepts/loaders,\nextending configurations, module.use, code splitting, tree shaking,\nauthor libraries, production, HMR concepts and the glossary.\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies (#8340)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies within their semver ranges\n\nIncludes webpack 5.107 -> 5.110, prettier 3.8 -> 3.9, cypress 15.12 ->\n15.21, react-router-dom 7.13 -> 7.18 and the rest of the in-range\nupdates. Prettier 3.9 prints a block whose only content is a comment on\none line, which reformats four documentation code samples.\n\n* chore(deps): update feed, webpack-dev-server and @docsearch/react to v6, v6 and v5\n\nDocSearch v5 replaces the `indexName` prop with an `indices` array, so\nNavigation passes the configured index as a single-element array. The\noverridden button class names and the primary-color variable are\nunchanged in v5, and the entry bundle drops from 1.06 MiB to 901 KiB.\n\n* chore(deps): update Babel to v8\n\nBabel 8 drops @babel/plugin-proposal-class-properties, whose transform\npreset-env now applies on its own, so the plugin goes with it.\n\n* chore(deps): match the react-router range to react-router-dom\n\nreact-router-dom 7.18.2 depends on exactly react-router 7.18.2, so the\ndeclared range now says so.\n\n* chore(deps): raise the Node requirement to match the updated toolchain\n\nBabel 8 requires Node ^22.18.0 || >=24.11.0 and webpack-dev-server 6\nrequires >=22.15.0, so the declared range no longer described what the\ndependencies install on.\n\n* chore(deps): hold @docsearch/react at v4\n\nv5 ships an Ask AI feature whose dependency chain (ai, @ai-sdk/*) brings\nin undici, which carries a high-severity advisory, so dependency-review\nrejects it. Holding the upgrade drops the chain, takes the audit from 26\nvulnerabilities on main to 12, and leaves the production build without\nthe warning @ai-sdk/provider-utils was emitting.\n\n* docs: document the webpack 5.110.0 configuration and API surface (#8337)\n\n* docs(performance): document the 5.110 performance checks\n\nAdds performance.all, hints: \"stats\" and the opt-in checks introduced in\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus an overview table grouping them by what they\ninspect and a note on which ones are not gated on hints.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(module): document Rule.glob and Rule.descriptionRelativePath\n\nBoth conditions land in webpack 5.110.0: glob matches the resource\nOS-independently and is also accepted inside a Condition object, and\ndescriptionRelativePath matches a module by its path inside its own\npackage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(externals): document nodeModules preset and external sideEffects\n\nCovers externalsPresets.nodeModules and its allowlist, which replace the\nwebpack-node-externals plugin, plus the { external, sideEffects } value\nform, both added in webpack 5.110.0. Also fills in the bun and deno\npreset rows, which the table was missing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(output): document contained path placeholders, umdAmdContainer, resourceHints.dedupe and per-entry html\n\nAdds the [containedfile]/[containedpath] template placeholders,\noutput.library.umdAmdContainer and output.resourceHints.dedupe from\nwebpack 5.110.0, plus the entry descriptor''s html option, which now\naccepts an object overriding output.html per entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): document minimize per asset type\n\nwebpack 5.110.0 makes optimization.minimize accept an object that\nconfigures the built-in minimizer per asset type, and the default\nminimizer now handles CSS and HTML too. Documents the javascript, css\nand html option sets and when each minifier runs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(stats): document stats.hints and stats.hintsCount\n\nAlso adds the deferImport and sourceImport environment flags to the\noutput.environment listing, both added in webpack 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(api): document __webpack_css_server_styles__ and MultiCompiler hooks\n\nThe module variable reads back the CSS collected while rendering without\na DOM, and MultiCompiler gained an aggregated shutdown hook plus a done\nhook that reports which compilers actually rebuilt. Both in 5.110.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: document renderEmbeddedSource and HTML head hot patching\n\nAdds the renderEmbeddedSource and embeddedSourceHash compilation hooks,\nand updates the HTML HMR note: 5.110.0 patches the head in place instead\nof falling back to a full page reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(performance): fix dataUrlCondition link target\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(optimization): keep main''s inline comment formatting\n\nThe local prettier (3.8.3) reformatted two of main''s inline block\ncomments onto their own lines; the declared version (3.9.6), which CI\ninstalls, wants them inline, which is how they are committed on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: state what CSS and HTML support is built in, and use it in the guides (#8342)\n\n* docs: state what built-in CSS and HTML actually cover\n\nThe loaders and plugins indexes called style-loader, css-loader,\nhtml-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and HtmlWebpackPlugin deprecated and\nsuperseded, which overstates it: the built-in support is experimental and\ndoes not cover preprocessors, css-loader''s importLoaders, localIdentRegExp,\ngetJSON and filter callbacks, style-loader''s insert, attributes,\nstyleTagTransform and lazy/singleton injection, html-loader''s\nscriptingEnabled and postprocessor, or html-webpack-plugin''s chunksSortMode,\nxhtml, showErrors, cache and plugin-hook ecosystem.\n\nAdd a \"What''s built-in\" section to both guides stating the scope as two\ncolumns, and point the index entries at it instead of declaring the\npackages superseded. Also scope the favicon claim: webpack emits the icons\nit is given, it does not generate size and format variants.\n\n* docs: say what needs no loader, and keep the list entries short\n\nA developer scanning the loaders list cannot tell which capabilities\nwebpack already has, so lead with the list of what needs no loader:\nJavaScript, JSON, asset modules, WebAssembly, and the experimental CSS,\nHTML and TypeScript support.\n\nShorten the entries added for the CSS and HTML loaders to a single\nparenthetical, so the list reads as a list again; the scope of each\nbuilt-in stays in the guide it links to.\n\n* docs: lead the loaders page with what needs no loader\n\nMove the list above the introduction so it is the first thing on the\npage, and fold the closing line into the prose that follows it.\n\n* docs: replace html-webpack-plugin with output.html in the guides\n\nEight pages now generate their page with output.html instead of the\nplugin: the development, HMR, production, PWA and modern web platform\nguides, the two concepts pages that used the plugin only as an example of\nwhat a plugin is, and the CoffeeScript configuration sample. Each keeps\nits title through output.html.title and pins the page name with\noutput.htmlFilename, since the default derives it from output.filename.\n\nOutput management and caching keep the plugin, with a note saying why:\noutput.html re-enters the entry''s script under an internal chunk name and\nleaves the named entry chunk holding the page, so a guide whose subject is\nbundle filenames would be teaching the wrong thing.\n\n* docs: enable html where html-webpack-plugin was replaced\n\nDropping the plugin is only half the change: the configuration has to keep\ngenerating the page. Three examples lost HTML generation entirely when the\nplugin was removed — the two concepts pages and the CoffeeScript config —\nand the guides that did set output.html leaned on the ''auto'' default\ninstead of saying so.\n\nEvery one of them now enables experiments.html and sets output.html, so\neach configuration does what it did with the plugin.\n\n* docs: only convert the examples whose output output.html reproduces\n\nBuilt each converted config both ways and compared the emitted files, which\nturned up four mismatches:\n\n- The three examples that passed `template` to the plugin were converted to\n  output.html, which generates a bare document and threw the template''s lang,\n  charset, title and body away. They now use an HTML entry point, which keeps\n  the authored page and rewrites its script URL.\n- The generated page carried no charset or viewport, which the plugin emits by\n  default; output.html.meta now supplies both.\n- production emitted app.html and modern web platform emitted a page whose name\n  carried the contenthash, because both derive from output.filename. Both now\n  pin output.htmlFilename to index.html.\n- The multi-entry guides — development, HMR and PWA — emit one page per\n  entrypoint instead of the single page the plugin builds, six files where\n  there were three, and development prints that file list in six places. They\n  keep the plugin, with the same note output management and caching carry.\n\n* docs: add ESM and CommonJS interoperability resource (#8343)\n\nAdd a focused ESM/CommonJS semantics and interoperability resource to Further Reading.\n\n* docs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post (#8338)\n\n* docs(blog): add the webpack 5.110 release post\n\nCovers the performance hint suite, built-in CSS and HTML minification,\nthe native CSS story, the nodeModules externals preset, the glob rule\ncondition and the rest of the release.\n\nThe benchmark table comparing the native pipeline with the loader one is\na placeholder pending real measurements, and the banner image still has\nto be added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): point the CSS migration at the new codemod\n\nwebpack/codemods ships @webpack/css-plugins-to-native-css, which does\nthe mini-css-extract-plugin and style-loader/css-loader migration the\npost describes by hand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): drop the empty benchmark table\n\nThe Benchmarks section keeps its placeholder note until the real\nmeasurements are in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): replace the benchmark section with the performance claim\n\nDrops the empty Benchmarks section and its table of contents entry, and\nsays instead where the win comes from: the built-in support parses each\nstylesheet once as CSS instead of once per loader plus once as a\nJavaScript module, so a build whose work is mostly CSS gains the most.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): mention the devtool default change for library builds\n\nA module or modern-module library, and any library under\nfutureDefaults, no longer gets the default eval source map in\ndevelopment, since the eval wrapper hides import.meta from the bundler\nreading the library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): add the release banner and move the post to today\n\nBuilds the banner in the style of the 5.108 and 5.109 ones: the webpack\nlockup from src/assets/logo-on-dark-bg.svg, Geomanist for the type, and\nthe same palette, sizes and layout measured off webpack-5-109.png.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(blog): fix the codemod command\n\nThe Codemod CLI takes the package directly; ''run'' is not part of it.\nMatches the command the Native CSS guide already documents, which the\npost now links to for the full option mapping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes (#8344)\n\n* docs: drop the built-in-superseded loaders and plugins from the indexes\n\ncss-loader, style-loader, html-loader, MiniCssExtractPlugin and\nHtmlWebpackPlugin are no longer listed on /loaders/ and /plugins/, the\nsame treatment file-loader, url-loader and raw-loader got when asset\nmodules replaced them. Each page stays reachable and is linked from the\nnote that replaces its entry, so the options with no built-in equivalent\nare still documented.\n\n* docs: stop pointing readers at the superseded loaders and plugins\n\nThe guide series builds its CSS with the built-in support, so production''s\ndevDependencies listed css-loader and style-loader that nothing installs.\noutput.mdx sent readers to css-loader''s docs for localIdentName, which\nwebpack has as a generator option. The UseEntry and kebab-case examples\nand the awesome-webpack ecosystem list named them where any loader would\ndo.\n\n* build: use webpack''s built-in CSS instead of css-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin\n\nThe site documents native CSS but did not use it. The rule keeps\npostcss-loader for Tailwind and hands the result to webpack via\ntype: css/auto; output.cssFilename reproduces the plugin''s names.\n\nVerified against the previous config: 382 emitted files and 188 pages\nboth ways, the vendor stylesheet byte-identical (97fc31c3662cb803), and\nindex.css differing by two bytes because webpack quotes the @import url.\nThe stray stylesheet the SSG pass emits drops from 48.6 KB to 177 B.\n\n* build: minify CSS with webpack instead of css-minimizer-webpack-plugin\n\nwebpack minifies CSS itself and deliberately steps aside when another\nminimizer claims those assets, so the plugin was displacing it. Dropping\nit is a gzip win on both stylesheets: vendor 5939 -> 5884 B and the main\nsheet 13181 -> 13130 B, 106 B less over the wire.\n\nThe ssg pass replaced the default minimizers rather than extending them,\nso its server bundle was never minified and the stylesheet it emits is\nunreferenced; it now says minimize: false instead.\n\nAll 188 pages stay byte-identical and the emitted file list is unchanged.\n\n* build: update webpack to 5.110.2\n\n* docs(performance): document the grouped hint options (#8350)\n\n* docs(performance): document the grouped hint options\n\n* docs(performance): name the renamed checks and the federation ones\n\nThe seven names 5.110.0 shipped were removed when the checks were grouped,\nand webpack rejects an unknown property, so a config still using one fails\nvalidation rather than being ignored. Give them a table pointing at what\nreplaced each.\n\nAlso record that `unusedConfig` now covers Module Federation, including the\ncase that stays silent today: an exact `shared` key matches only the exact\nrequest, so it shares nothing next to a deep import.\n\n* docs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it (#8353)\n\n* docs(config): document output.copy and the CopyPlugin behind it\n\nwebpack copies files itself since 5.111.0. Adds the output.copy reference\nwith its pattern, glob and transform options, a CopyPlugin page for the\nconcurrency and stage options output.copy does not carry, and lists the\nplugin in the index, marking copy-webpack-plugin as superseded.\n\n* fix(ci): satisfy the sort lint rule and point the index at lint-webpack-plugin\n\nThe CopyPlugin merge example sorted with Array#sort, which unicorn/no-array-sort\nrejects; toSorted does the same on the array filter already returned.\n\nThe link check was failing on /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin, which the plugins\nindex still lists. webpack/eslint-webpack-plugin was renamed to\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin (it now runs ESLint and Stylelint and replaces\nstylelint-webpack-plugin too), so the org listing the page generator walks no\nlonger carries the old name and no page is built for it. The entry now names the\nrenamed plugin. This failure predates the branch — it reproduces on unrelated\nPRs — but it blocks this one, so it is fixed here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(plugins): follow the rename to diagnostics-webpack-plugin\n\nThe plugin that replaced eslint-webpack-plugin and stylelint-webpack-plugin was\nrenamed again, from lint-webpack-plugin to diagnostics-webpack-plugin, since it\nnow covers type checkers and other diagnostic tools rather than linters alone.\nThe org listing the plugin pages are generated from carries only the new name,\nso the index entry follows it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n* fix(build): only link a README''s package when the site builds its page\n\nprocess-readme rewrote every github.com/webpack{,-contrib}/*-loader and\n*-plugin URL into an internal docs link, whether or not a page for that\npackage exists. stylelint-webpack-plugin''s README points at\nwebpack/lint-webpack-plugin, which has since been renamed again, so the\ngenerated page carried a link to /plugins/lint-webpack-plugin/ and the link\ncheck failed on it.\n\nThe rewrite is now gated on the repository lists the pages are generated\nfrom, which fetch-package-readmes passes in: a package missing from them\nkeeps its GitHub link, which redirects to wherever the repository moved,\ninstead of pointing at a page that was never built. Without the lists the\nbehaviour is unchanged, so processReadme keeps working on its own.\n\nAlso strips the trailing slash a matched URL may carry before building the\ninternal path and comparing against the exclusion lists, which those two\ncomparisons already assumed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(performance): document performance.analyzableBailouts (#8351)\n\nNames the option, what it reports and what lifts each reason it can print,\nincluding that an eval devtool hides even the specifiers webpack writes out.\n\n* docs(awesome-webpack): follow the rename to diagnostics-webpack-plugin (#8354)\n\nwebpack-contrib/eslint-webpack-plugin is now\nwebpack/diagnostics-webpack-plugin, which runs ESLint, Stylelint and other\ndiagnostic tools from one plugin, so the entry names what the package is\ntoday rather than relying on the GitHub redirect.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KLzwNGe4rDGGQi3gzGEZyv\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: teach the docs native HTML and CSS, drop html-webpack-plugin and the CSS loaders (#8355)\n\n* docs: drop html-webpack-plugin from the guides and reference\n\nThe guide series taught HtmlWebpackPlugin and each page carried a note\nexplaining why it had not moved to the built-in HTML support yet. Webpack\nbuilds pages itself, so the guides now use it and the plugin is no longer\nnamed anywhere outside the migration guide.\n\noutput-management makes src/index.html the entry point: the page lists the\nscripts it needs, webpack rewrites their URLs to the emitted bundles, and\nthere is no second list of entry points to keep in sync. development, HMR\nand PWA follow that config through, and caching uses output.html since it\nkeeps a single JavaScript entry. Every build listing in those guides was\nregenerated against webpack 5.110.3.\n\nScripts a page references become chunks of that page, so their names are\ngenerated (__html_<hash>_<n>) rather than taken from entry. That is what\nthe listings show now, with a note in output-management and caching saying\nwhere the names come from.\n\n/plugins/html-webpack-plugin is removed and redirects to the Native HTML\nguide, which documents the plugin''s options and their built-in equivalents.\nThe plugins index links there instead of to the deleted page.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: build the front page example with native HTML and CSS\n\nThe splash example bundled one JavaScript file and asked the reader to\nwrite the page by hand, pointing a <script> tag at dist/bundle.js. Webpack\nhandles all three now, so the example starts from src/index.html: the page\nlinks a stylesheet and a script, entry points at the page, and the emitted\ndocument is shown next to the config with its URLs rewritten to the hashed\nassets. Verified against webpack 5.110.3 — an HTML entry turns on the html\nand css support on its own, and htmlFilename keeps the page''s name out of\nthe contenthash pattern.\n\nThe migration guide''s companion-plugin table now covers the popular\nhtml-webpack-plugin ecosystem rather than five entries, and a new section\nmaps its six hooks onto HtmlModulesPlugin''s, with a plugin rewritten\nthrough transformTags and injectTags as the worked example.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: drop css-loader, style-loader and MiniCssExtractPlugin from the docs\n\nWebpack handles CSS itself, so the three packages are no longer named\noutside the migration guide, and their pages are gone: css-loader and\nstyle-loader join the excluded loaders, MiniCssExtractPlugin the excluded\nplugins, and /loaders/css-loader, /loaders/style-loader and\n/plugins/mini-css-extract-plugin redirect to the Native CSS guide. The\nexclusion entries carry the webpack/ prefix the repositories actually\nhave; the older webpack-contrib/ spellings around them no longer match\nanything the fetcher lists.\n\nThe HMR guide stops installing style-loader and css-loader for its\nstylesheet section: experiments.css defaults to ''auto'', so importing a\nstylesheet needs no rule at all — webpack bundles it and links it into the\npage, verified against webpack 5.110.3. The remaining mentions were\nreference asides (a filter option, an ident-hash comment, an exports\nconvention, the CSS extraction bullet) and now describe the behavior\nwithout naming a package, linking the guide where a reader needs more.\n\nLeft alone: the Native CSS migration guide, which has to name what it\nmigrates from, and the release posts and the v1-to-v2 migration guide,\nwhere the loaders are part of the record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs: name a page''s bundles after its entry in the build listings\n\nwebpack/webpack#22008 gives a page''s extracted scripts the entry''s\nfilename now that the page emits no JavaScript of its own, so the guides\nstop showing generated identifiers. output-management and development list\nmain.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js for the two scripts the page pulls in,\nthe PWA listing follows in the same format, and caching is back to\nmain.<contenthash>.js beside runtime and vendors — its note about generated\nchunk names is gone and the prose names the main bundle again.\n\nEvery listing was regenerated against that branch (84c1155): a page with\ntwo scripts emits main.bundle.js and main1.bundle.js, and the caching setup\nemits main.<hash>.js, vendors.<hash>.js and runtime.<hash>.js.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* test: use postcss-loader as the package the site has a page for\n\nThe two owner-rename tests used css-loader as their example, and this\nbranch stops building a css-loader page, so the \"has a page\" assertion\nno longer holds. postcss-loader is the same shape — a webpack-owned\nloader the site still builds a page for — and keeps both tests testing\nwhat they were written for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n* docs(config): document the validate option\n\ndiagnostics-webpack-plugin''s README links to\n/configuration/other-options/#validate, and the anchor did not exist:\nwebpack has had a top-level `validate` option since 5.106.0, and this\npage never covered it. That dead fragment fails the link check on any\nbuild, this branch included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NuWDbcF2jvq7q1r8aEY5V9\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: give every page its own meta description (#8361)\n\n* docs: give every page its own meta description\n\nAll 136 non-blog pages shared one fallback meta description, so every page\nemitted an identical <meta name=\"description\"> and og:description. Duplicate\ndescriptions give search engines and retrieval pipelines no per-page signal,\nand Google discards them in favour of a synthesized snippet.\n\nAdd a description to each of the 132 pages that lacked one, and rewrite the\nfallback in Site.jsx. Both now reflect what webpack actually bundles and what\nit targets: JavaScript, CSS, HTML, WebAssembly and assets, for browsers,\nNode.js, Deno, Bun and other environments, rather than \"JavaScript files for\nusage in a browser\".\n\nDescriptions name the concrete options and superseded packages a reader\nsearches for, following the pattern already used by the native CSS and HTML\nguides.\n\nAlso list CSS and HTML in the native module types on concepts/modules, which\nstill enumerated only ECMAScript, CommonJS, AMD, assets and WebAssembly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n* test: assert the home page''s own meta description\n\ncheck-server-side-rendering pinned the old fallback string and visited \"/\"\nto read it. The home page now carries its own description, so \"/\" no longer\nrenders the fallback at all and the assertion was stale twice over.\n\nPoint the assertion at the home page''s actual description and rename the\ncase to match what it covers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LDxiMfJ9FnjuLdeRkwdWPa\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump the dependencies group across 1 directory with 11 updates (#8363)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 11 updates in the / directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [react-router-dom](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/tree/HEAD/packages/react-router-dom) | `7.18.2` | `7.18.3` |\n| [@octokit/auth-action](https://github.com/octokit/auth-action.js) | `6.0.2` | `6.0.3` |\n| [@testing-library/react](https://github.com/testing-library/react-testing-library) | `16.3.2` | `16.3.3` |\n| [autoprefixer](https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer) | `10.5.4` | `10.5.5` |\n| [globals](https://github.com/sindresorhus/globals) | `17.11.0` | `17.12.0` |\n| [jest](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/tree/HEAD/packages/jest) | `30.4.2` | `30.5.1` |\n| [jest-environment-jsdom](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/tree/HEAD/packages/jest-environment-jsdom) | `30.4.1` | `30.5.1` |\n| [lint-staged](https://github.com/lint-staged/lint-staged) | `17.4.1` | `17.5.0` |\n| [postcss](https://github.com/postcss/postcss) | `8.5.26` | `8.5.28` |\n| [webpack](https://github.com/webpack/webpack) | `5.110.2` | `5.110.3` |\n| [webpack-cli](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-cli) | `7.2.2` | `7.2.3` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `react-router-dom` from 7.18.2 to 7.18.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/blob/react-router-dom@7.18.3/packages/react-router-dom/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/commits/react-router-dom@7.18.3/packages/react-router-dom)\n\nUpdates `@octokit/auth-action` from 6.0.2 to 6.0.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/octokit/auth-action.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/octokit/auth-action.js/compare/v6.0.2...v6.0.3)\n\nUpdates `@testing-library/react` from 16.3.2 to 16.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/testing-library/react-testing-library/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/testing-library/react-testing-library/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/testing-library/react-testing-library/compare/v16.3.2...v16.3.3)\n\nUpdates `autoprefixer` from 10.5.4 to 10.5.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer/compare/10.5.4...10.5.5)\n\nUpdates `globals` from 17.11.0 to 17.12.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/sindresorhus/globals/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/sindresorhus/globals/compare/v17.11.0...v17.12.0)\n\nUpdates `jest` from 30.4.2 to 30.5.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/commits/v30.5.1/packages/jest)\n\nUpdates `jest-environment-jsdom` from 30.4.1 to 30.5.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/commits/v30.5.1/packages/jest-environment-jsdom)\n\nUpdates `lint-staged` from 17.4.1 to 17.5.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/lint-staged/lint-staged/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/lint-staged/lint-staged/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/lint-staged/lint-staged/compare/v17.4.1...v17.5.0)\n\nUpdates `postcss` from 8.5.26 to 8.5.28\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/postcss/postcss/compare/8.5.26...8.5.28)\n\nUpdates `webpack` from 5.110.2 to 5.110.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/compare/v5.110.2...v5.110.3)\n\nUpdates `webpack-cli` from 7.2.2 to 7.2.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-cli/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-cli/compare/webpack-cli@7.2.2...webpack-cli@7.2.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: react-router-dom\n  dependency-version: 7.18.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: \"@octokit/auth-action\"\n  dependency-version: 6.0.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: \"@testing-library/react\"\n  dependency-version: 16.3.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: autoprefixer\n  dependency-version: 10.5.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: globals\n  dependency-version: 17.12.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: jest\n  dependency-version: 30.5.1\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: jest-environment-jsdom\n  dependency-version: 30.5.1\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: lint-staged\n  dependency-version: 17.5.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: postcss\n  dependency-version: 8.5.28\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: webpack\n  dependency-version: 5.110.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n- dependency-name: webpack-cli\n  dependency-version: 7.2.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update changes\n\n* docs(loaders): clarify module-level cacheability (#8352)\n\n* docs: fix outdated references in glossary and comparison (#8356)\n\n* docs: correct plugin and loader authoring contribute guidance (#8359)\n\n* docs: correct outdated guides and inaccurate statements (#8362)\n\n* docs: correct outdated guides and inaccurate statements\n\n* lint\n\n* docs: correct api hook types, signatures and removed APIs (#8364)\n\n* docs: correct migration guidance that no longer matches webpack 5 (#8365)\n\n* docs: answer long-standing questions about inaccurate or missing reference docs (#8367)\n\n* docs(configuration): explain chunk loading global, snapshot paths and mode defaults\n\nAnswer the questions the open documentation issues ask: what\noutput.chunkLoadingGlobal is and when to set it, which info properties a\ndevtoolModuleFilenameTemplate function receives, how snapshot.managedPaths\ndiffers from immutablePaths, which module type reads Rule.parser.parse,\nwhich defaults each mode picks, what the deterministic id plugins accept\nand what resolve starts from.\n\n* docs(api): document dynamic import expressions, eager mode and rootContext\n\nA fully dynamic import() builds an empty context rather than being\nimpossible, webpackChunkName does nothing in eager mode, and\nthis.rootContext was described by its history instead of its meaning.\n\n* docs(plugins): correct eval source map filters and expand federation sharing\n\nEvalSourceMapDevToolPlugin matches modules, not assets, and emits no map\nfiles. Also define initial and async chunks for splitChunks.chunks, and\nsay what shareKey, shareScope and a unique name are for.\n\n* docs(plugins): explain what PrefetchPlugin does and what it is not\n\nIt shortens the build''s critical path and is unrelated to the browser\nresource hint people reach for it expecting.\n\n* docs: correct plugin option defaults, signatures and removed CLI flags (#8357)\n\n* docs: correct outdated concepts and inaccurate statements (#8358)\n\nCo-authored-by: Alexander Akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* doc: correct configuration statements (#8366)\n\n* docs: document the API surface that had no docs at all (#8368)\n\nAn audit of webpack''s schemas, hook definitions, APIPlugin and loader\ncontext against every heading on the site found options, hooks and module\nvariables that are reachable but undocumented. Adds the missing Compiler,\nCompilation and JavascriptParser hooks, optimization.minimizeOptions, five\nRule conditions, four javascript parser options, six module variables,\nthis.addBuildDependency, the CacheFacade and the module/chunk graph APIs\nwith their deprecation replacements.\n\n* docs: document intermediateFileSystem, id plugins, rule merging and serialization (#8369)\n\nFollow-up from triaging the webpack 5 alpha documentation requests: the\ncompiler''s three file systems, the webpack.ids.* plugins behind each\nmoduleIds/chunkIds value, how Rule.resolve and Rule.parser arrays merge\nwith ''...'', getParentModule, and how a plugin''s own classes are made\ncacheable.\n\n* docs: document container plugin options, shared version ranges, ts-node overrides and conditional polyfills (#8370)\n\nCovers the remaining documentation requests that name a real, checkable\nbehavior: the ContainerPlugin and ContainerReferencePlugin options, the\nsemver range grammar requiredVersion accepts and how several versions\ncoexist in a share scope, ts-node''s own TS_NODE_PROJECT and moduleTypes,\nand an example of serving a smaller polyfill bundle to modern browsers.\n\n* docs: document plugin typing, loader-to-plugin data, condition composition and non-ES5 dependencies (#8371)\n\n* docs: add Module Object page, document deploy chunk load errors and HMR record persistence (#8372)\n\n* docs: explain loader restarts in watch mode and HMR in generated loader output (#8373)\n\n* docs: add HMR patterns for side effects, state, singletons and server-side updates (#8374)\n\n* docs: correct HMR bubbling model and document update files on the wire (#8375)\n\n* fix: keep service worker installable when an asset cannot be precached (#8376)\n\n* fix: give the governance docs their own sidebar section (#8378)\n\n* docs: group the plugins index by purpose and list the missing plugin pages (#8377)\n\n* docs: replace the removed overridables model with how share scopes actually work (#8379)\n\n* docs: document name, filename and remotes, and who loads a container (#8380)\n\n* docs: add a Compiler Object page (#8381)\n\n* docs: use TypeScript notation for types in the writer''s guide (#8382)\n\n* docs: migrate the remaining pages to TypeScript notation (#8383)\n\n* docs(configuration): migrate configuration pages to TypeScript notation\n\n* docs(configuration): migrate entry, externals and dev-server to TypeScript notation\n\n* docs(api): migrate API object pages to TypeScript notation\n\n* docs(plugins): migrate plugin and concept pages to TypeScript notation\n\n* docs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar (#8384)\n\n* docs: drop deprecated loaders and plugins from the sidebar\n\nEvery webpack-org loader and plugin page the site builds now comes from a\nrepository that is not archived. The eleven archived ones are excluded from\nthe fetch and their URLs redirect to what replaced them: native HTML, the\nbuilt-in CopyPlugin, MinimizerPlugin or DiagnosticsWebpackPlugin.\n\nAlso redirects /plugins/terser-webpack-plugin and /plugins/eslint-webpack-plugin,\nwhich 404 since those repositories were renamed.\n\n* docs: teach the shimming guide webpack''s own imports/exports recipe\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections taught imports-loader and\nexports-loader, both deprecated. They now use the plugin from webpack''s\nadd-imports and add-exports examples, so neither loader is mentioned anywhere\nin the docs.\n\nThe Granular Shimming example also never demonstrated the problem: it read\n`this` inside a function called bare, which is already the global object in a\nsloppy module. It now reads the module''s own `this`, which is what the wrapper\nchanges.\n\ncopy-webpack-plugin redirects to output.copy, and the two loader URLs to the\nsections that replace them.\n\n* docs: link webpack''s examples instead of inlining the shim plugin\n\nThe Granular Shimming and Global Exports sections point at the add-imports\nand add-exports examples rather than carrying a copy of the plugin, which\nwould go stale against the examples it was taken from.\n\n* docs: stop naming deprecated loaders and plugins outside the migration guides\n\nA developer reading the docs should meet the built-in feature, not the package\nit replaced. The remaining mentions in guides, configuration and API pages are\nreworded to describe the behaviour, and the three archived webpack packages are\ndropped from the awesome-webpack list.\n\nThe Native CSS and Native HTML guides keep theirs: naming what you are moving\noff is the point of a migration guide.\n\n* docs: say which hook a plugin creates assets in (#8385)\n\nThe compiler''s emit hook runs after the compilation is sealed, so an asset\nadded there skips every processAssets stage and webpack reports the write as\ndeprecated. Nothing in the docs said so, and the plugins concept page had no\nguidance for plugin authors at all.\n\nCloses #2864\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies (#8386)\n\n* chore(deps): update dependencies\n\nUpdates everything that can move without an upstream block or a code\nmigration: babel, react 19.3, eslint-config-webpack, autoprefixer,\nlint-staged, webpack-bundle-analyzer, react-refresh 0.19, cypress 16 and\n@docsearch/react 5.\n\nThree are left where they are, each for a reason outside this repo:\n\n- eslint 10 - eslint-plugin-react''s latest (7.37.5) peer-caps at eslint\n  ^9.7 and calls context.getFilename(), which eslint 10 removed.\n- eslint-plugin-cypress 7 - requires eslint >= 10, so it waits on the above.\n- react-router 8 - react-router-dom has no v8 and hard-pins react-router\n  7.18.3, so v8 means migrating every import off react-router-dom; v8 is\n  also ESM only and the jest suites cannot load it as CommonJS.\n\n* chore(deps): keep @docsearch/react on 4.x\n\nv5 replaces the single indexName prop with an indices array, so the\nNavigation component throws \"Must supply at least one `indices` entry for\nDocSearch\" on every page. That is an API migration rather than a version\nbump, so it goes with react-router 8 into a PR of its own.\n\n* chore(deps): keep cypress on 15.x\n\nCypress 16 runs Chrome on the native browser network instead of routing\nthrough Cypress, and 16.0.0 has two service-worker regressions fixed only\nin an unreleased 16.0.1. The site registers a Workbox service worker whose\ncatch handler falls back to the empty app shell, so scroll.cy.js loses the\npage content it asserts on.\n\n* chore(deps): drop autoprefixer\n\nwebpack''s CSS minifier maintains vendor prefixes from the same browserslist,\nadding what a target needs and stripping what none does. Feeding it the\nautoprefixed stylesheet and the unprefixed one emits byte-identical CSS, so\nautoprefixer never reached the bundle. Site CSS is 11 gzip bytes larger: three\ninert -webkit-backdrop-filter entries in transition-property lists that\nautoprefixer used to prune.\n\nThe native CSS guide already documents this.\n\n* chore(deps): drop lightningcss\n\nNothing imports it. It came in with css-loader, mini-css-extract-plugin and\ncss-minimizer-webpack-plugin, whose minifier it backed; those went when the\nsite moved to experiments.css and this stayed. @tailwindcss/postcss carries\nits own nested copy, so Tailwind is unaffected, and npm ci stops fetching a\nsecond set of native binaries.\n\nOn the site''s stylesheet webpack''s minifier emits 45923 raw / 9811 gzip\nagainst lightningcss''s 46880 / 9845.\n\n* chore(deps): update @docsearch/react to 5 (#8389)\n\nv5 replaces the indexName prop with an indices array; every other prop the\nNavigation component passes survives unchanged. The button, modal and input\nselectors the stylesheet and search.cy.js rely on are unchanged too: the\ninput id is still built as docsearch-input by autocomplete-core''s\ngetAutocompleteElementId, and all six .DocSearch-* hooks the site overrides\nare still in @docsearch/css.\n\nThe entry payload shrinks: vendor.js 766422 -> 560608 raw and 208944 ->\n170637 gzip, against +18012 raw / +2495 gzip of DocSearch stylesheet, for\n301857 -> 263594 gzip over the entrypoint''s js and css.\n\n* chore(deps): update react-router to 8 and drop react-router-dom (#8391)\n\nreact-router-dom has no v8 and hard-pins react-router 7, so v8 means moving\nevery import onto react-router itself. All ten APIs the site uses are exported\nfrom it.\n\nv8 is ESM only, with no require condition and no CommonJS build, so jest\nrefuses to require it whatever babel does with it - the component tests have to\nbe ESM. Eleven of the fourteen already imported from @jest/globals and needed\nno change; the four using jest.mock now use unstable_mockModule with a dynamic\nimport. _supporters.json is generated and absent in CI, and a virtual mock has\nno ESM equivalent because the import graph resolves before anything runs, so it\nis mapped to an empty fixture that the tests needing data override. Page''s\nrouter mock is gone: it pinned useLocation to /test, which MemoryRouter''s\ninitialEntries does on its own.\n\neslint-import-resolver-node predates exports maps and v8 declares no main, so\nimport/no-unresolved cannot find it and is scoped to ignore that one specifier.\n\n* docs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks (#8387)\n\n* docs(output): say where an ESM build names its chunks\n\n`output.chunkFilename` still described the chunk id to filename map as the only\nway a chunk is named. Since 5.111.0 an `output.module` build loading through a\nnative `import()` holds a literal specifier per chunk in the chunk loader, so the\nname is in the runtime chunk rather than in every module importing it.\n\nDrops the analyzable-bailout row for a chunk the compilation emits no javascript\nfor, which is no longer reported: such a chunk is simply left out of that map.\n\n* docs(output): keep the chunk naming note under the line limit\n\nmarkdownlint caps a line at 600 characters and the note ran to 715.\n\n* docs: mark experiments.outputModule removed, document output.module alone (#8360)\n\nESM output is stable in webpack 5.111.0, so `output.module` no longer\nneeds an experiment behind it.\n\n* docs: add a build lifecycle overview to Under The Hood (#8393)\n\nCloses #2223. The page described what a build is made of - modules, chunks,\nassets - but never the order they are produced in, which is what plugin\nauthors and config readers were asking for.\n\nAdds the phase pipeline from compiler creation through run, compile, make,\nseal, emit and done, with the hooks that mark each phase, plus a short note\non what make and seal actually do and a table pointing common tasks at the\nhook that serves them. Every hook name and its position is taken from\nCompiler.run/compile and Compilation.seal rather than from memory.\n\nLinks it from the plugins concept page, where a plugin author lands first.\n\n* docs(module): document the rest of module.parser.javascript (#8394)\n\nAn audit of schemas/WebpackOptions.json against the configuration pages found\n26 of the 49 JavascriptParserOptions had no documentation, and that the\nModule Contexts section taught the deprecated spelling of twelve of them.\n\nModule Contexts now shows the options where they actually live, under\nmodule.parser.javascript, and says that setting them on module directly is\ndeprecated and where each moved.\n\nAdds typescript, deferImport and sourceImport, which default from the\nmatching experiments, and a table for the syntax toggles. The table states\neach default rather than implying one: requireJs and system are off until\nset to true, and requireInclude warns that it is deprecated unless set\nexplicitly - read from AMDPlugin, CommonJsPlugin, SystemPlugin,\nRequireJsStuffPlugin, RequireIncludePlugin and defaults.js.\n\n* docs: document specNamespaceObject, resolve.resolver and resolve.fileSystem (#8395)\n\nA second pass over schemas/WebpackOptions.json, asking whether each option\nis documented rather than merely mentioned, left three real gaps once the\nfalse positives were checked by hand.\n\nmodule.parser.javascript.specNamespaceObject is new in 5.111.0 and was\nundocumented. resolve.resolver and resolve.fileSystem are the last two\nResolveOptions with no entry; webpack overwrites the latter with the\ncompiler''s input filesystem, so the section says so rather than implying\nit is configurable.\n\n* docs(output): document the futureDefaults module output default (#8396)\n\nwebpack 5.111.0 defaults `output.module` to true under\n`experiments.futureDefaults` wherever the target reads an ECMAScript module,\nso both pages now say what turns it on and what holds it back: a target\nwithout module support, a library type read out of a script, or an explicit\n`output.module`. The option''s own default line also picks up the `module` and\n`modern-module` library types, which turn it on without the experiment.\n\n* docs(api): document the runtime requirement hook maps and addEntry (#8397)\n\nComparing the hooks Compilation.js defines against the page left four with\nno entry: runtimeRequirementInModule, runtimeRequirementInChunk,\nruntimeRequirementInTree and addEntry. The three HookMaps are how a plugin\nattaches a runtime module, and additionalTreeRuntimeRequirements — the hook\nreached for alongside them — was already documented, so the page showed one\nhalf of a pair.\n\n* docs(api): document addRuntimeModule and addLazyRuntimeModule (#8398)\n\n* docs(api): document addRuntimeModule and addLazyRuntimeModule\n\nThe runtime requirement hooks documented in #8397 reach for both methods,\nbut neither had an entry anywhere on the site, so the examples pointed at\nAPI a reader could not look up.\n\n* docs(api): link the runtime requirement hooks to the methods they call\n\nThe hooks page named addRuntimeModule and addLazyRuntimeModule as plain\ntext because neither had an entry to point at; this PR adds them, so the\nmentions become links.\n\n* docs(api): document the remaining parser and module factory hooks (#8399)\n\nExtending the hooks-versus-source comparison past Compiler and Compilation:\nNormalModuleFactory was 12/14 and JavascriptParser 46/59. Adds the two\nfactory hooks (resolveInScheme, prepareModuleType) and the thirteen parser\nhooks that had no entry, so every hook those classes define is documented.\n\n* docs(api): document the loader context request accessors and dependency getters (#8400)\n\nThe loader context exposes currentRequest, previousRequest, remainingRequest,\nresourceFragment, getDependencies, getContextDependencies,\ngetMissingDependencies and getLogger, none of which had an entry on the\nLoader Interface page. Also rename the pitch method''s second parameter in the\nexamples to previousRequest, which is the name webpack passes it under.\n\n* docs: build modern and legacy bundles from one source with layers (#8401)\n\nAdds the differential-serving recipe the shimming guide was missing: an entry\nper layer so webpack walks the graph twice and issuerLayer picks the babel\ntargets and polyfills for each copy, plus the array-of-configurations form for\nwhen the modern build has to be emitted as real ECMAScript modules.\n\nAlso documents the polyfill entry array on the entry page, with what importing\nall of core-js/stable actually costs, and links both to the shimming guide.\n\n* docs: resolve.fileSystem is honored since webpack 5.111.0 (#8402)\n\nwebpack/webpack#22091 stopped webpack from assigning the compiler''s input\nfilesystem over a configured resolve.fileSystem, so the page''s warning that\nsetting it has no effect is true only up to 5.110.x. Documents the option as it\nnow behaves, keeps the older workaround as a version note, and says what still\ngoes through the compiler''s inputFileSystem.\n\n* docs(api): show what this.getOptions does with a schema (#8403)\n\nThe option schema argument had a one-line mention and no example, so loader\nauthors reach for schema-utils by hand instead. Adds a worked example with the\nerror webpack actually prints, says what additionalProperties and title each\ncontribute to that message, and notes the two things the example alone would\nget wrong: the check runs while the module is built, and it does not run at all\nwhen the validate option is off.\n\n* ci: catch typos with cspell, and fix the five it found (#8404)\n\nThe site had no spellchecker: vale runs proselint and Speciesism, neither of\nwhich checks spelling, so a misspelling only ever got caught by a reader. That\nis why refrence sat in the TypeScript guide for months while the PR fixing it\nwaited on a CLA.\n\nAdds cspell with a word list covering the site''s vocabulary, wires it into the\nlint script and the lint CI job, and fixes what it found: refrence, a\nConcatinating heading, nummber, testLolcalStorage and scollbar. The deliberate\nmisspellings that teach something -- cosnole in the development guide, prefx in\nthe loader options example, and webpack 1''s real OccurenceOrderPlugin -- get a\nfile-local cspell:ignore instead of a dictionary entry, so the same word\nelsewhere is still an error.\n\n* docs(config): say what each output.library.type generates (#8405)\n\nThe type list named nineteen values and the sections below explained them at\nuneven depth: ''self'' and ''umd2'' had no section at all, ''module'' pointed at a\n2021 progress thread instead of showing its output, ''modern-module'' had one\nsentence, and ''global'' showed a globalThis assignment that no default target\nemits.\n\nAdds a table summarizing every type in one line, the two missing sections, real\ninput/output for the module types, and the three assignments ''global'' actually\nemits per target. Every example was read off a build rather than written by\nhand.\n\n* fix: build blog teasers from prose only, and earn the ellipsis (#8406)\n\nThree of the ten blog teasers on /blog/ are the post''s MDX preamble rather than\nits text: the 5.108, 5.109 and 5.110 previews all read ''import banner from\n\"../../assets/blog/webpack-5-110.png\"; <img src={banner} alt=...''. The teaser\nkept every line that was not a heading, so imports, exports and JSX all counted\nas prose.\n\nAlso takes the ellipsis fix from #8201: the ''...'' was appended whether or not\nanything had been cut, which gives blog/index.mdx a four-dot teaser because its\ntext already ends in a period.\n\nTests cover both, plus the empty-body case that used to yield a bare ''...''.\n\n* docs(contribute): add the codebase overview from #1824 (#8407)\n\nIssue #1824 asked for two things in 2018: a contributing section in the docs\nand a codebase overview. The section has existed for years; the overview was\nnever written, so nothing on the site tells a would-be contributor how\nwebpack''s own source is laid out, and the site never linked to CONTRIBUTING.md\nor TESTING_DOCS.md at all.\n\nAdds a page mapping the five objects a build runs through, the three phases,\nwhat each lib/ directory holds, and how to find the code behind an option, a\nhook, a runtime symbol or an error. It links out to CONTRIBUTING.md and\nTESTING_DOCS.md for process and tests rather than restating them, which is what\nthe issue thread asked for.\n\n* blog: webpack 5.111 (#8388)\n\n* blog: webpack 5.110\n\n* blog: cover more merged changes in the 5.111 post\n\nAdds the release items merged after the post was drafted: output.module\nunder futureDefaults and for module library types, ESM star reexports of\nexternals, the smaller chunk-loading runtime and released compilation\ndata, parse-time bailouts surviving the cache, attribute minification by\nvalue, the CSS Modules @value fix, spec namespaces for synthesized\nmodules, and resolve.fileSystem.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: alexander-akait <4567934+alexander-akait@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(blog): keep the roadmaps below the release posts (#8409)\n\nThe blog list is ordered by date, so a roadmap published between two\nreleases sat among them: roadmap 2026 (2026-02-04) above webpack 5.105\n(2026-02-03). Group the roadmaps after every other post, where the date\ncomparison then orders them from the highest year down.\n\n* docs: match the splash script tag to what webpack emits (#8392)\n\n* docs: match the splash script tag to what webpack emits\n\nThe page showed <script type=\"module\" src> going in and a classic <script\nsrc> coming out, captioned as a URL rewrite, so it read as though webpack had\ndropped the module type. It had not: without output.module the emitted chunk\nis a classic IIFE, and webpack matches the tag to it - with output.module set\nit keeps type=\"module\" and emits an ES module chunk.\n\nShowing a classic tag makes the before and after differ only in the URL, which\nis what the caption claims. The emitted page is unchanged, same content hash.\n\n* docs: keep the splash page on ES modules end to end\n\nRather than downgrading the page''s script tag to match a classic bundle,\nturn the config into one that emits ES modules, so type=\"module\" survives\nthe build. Restores the module tag on the input and adds output.module with\na line saying why it is there.\n\nVerified: with this config webpack emits [javascript module] chunks and the\npage keeps <script type=module src=...>. The [contenthash].js template is\nunchanged - output.module does not force an extension.\n\n* docs: drop the removed outputModule experiment from the splash config\n\nexperiments.outputModule is gone in 5.111.0 - output.module carries ESM\noutput on its own now, per #8360. It appears nowhere in webpack''s lib/ or\nschemas/ any more, and the ''only allowed when experiments.outputModule is\nenabled'' check is gone with it. 5.111.0 is unreleased, so this is read from\nsource rather than run; the installed 5.110.3 still enforces the old rule.\n\n* docs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes (#8410)\n\n* docs(splash): run the build instead of naming the hashes\n\nThe front page spent three output options on content hashes and then\nshowed their digits in the emitted page, which nothing on the page needs\nand which no reader can reproduce. Since 5.111 names a page''s entries\nafter the urls its tags carry, the config is down to the one option the\npage''s `type=\"module\"` tag asks for, and the emitted names are the ones\nwebpack gives them.\n\nThe room that frees goes to the two commands a first build is actually\nmade of, which the page never showed.\n\n* docs(splash): say what each mode does to the output\n\n* docs(optimization): point the bail link at the option''s own page\n\nThe link went to /api/cli/#advanced-options, an anchor the CLI page no\nlonger carries — it documents no bail flag at all — so the link check\nfailed on the fragment. bail is documented under other-options, which is\nwhere the sentence meant to send the reader.\n\n* docs(splash): give each mode its own command and description\n\nOne block with both commands made the reader hold two commands in mind\nbefore either was explained. Each command now stands next to what it\ndoes to the output.\n\n* fix: render a readme''s relative links against its own branch (#8411)\n\n`processReadme` turns a raw readme url into the page it is rendered at so\nthat relative links resolve, and it did that by inserting `blob/` in front\nof the literal `master`:\n\n    .replace(/master/, \"blob/master\")\n\nA repository on `main` therefore got no `blob/` at all, and every relative\nlink in its readme resolved to `github.com/<owner>/<repo>/main/<path>`,\nwhich is not a url GitHub serves. Of the loader and plugin repositories\nthe site generates pages from, the nine sampled are all on `main` —\nincluding `diagnostics-webpack-plugin`, whose readme links `CHANGELOG.md`\nand `./LICENSE`.\n\nThe branch is read from the raw url now, whatever it is called, so the\nrendered url is built rather than patched. A repository or owner whose\nname contains `master` is no longer rewritten by accident either.\n\nThe suite pinned the old behaviour: \"rewrite relative url\" asserted the\n`main` url without `blob/` as what it should be. It asserts the link that\nresolves now, and a new case covers `master`, `main` and `next` together.\n\n* Update changes\n\n* Update changes\n\n* docs: compression-webpack-plugin is folded into minimizer-webpack-plugin (#8415)\n\nIts page redirects to the section showing compression with and without minifying, the way the other folded minimizers already do.\n\n* chore(deps): bump cypress-io/github-action in the dependencies group (#8416)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 1 update: [cypress-io/github-action](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action).\n\n\nUpdates `cypress-io/github-action` from 7.4.3 to 7.4.4\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/cypress-io/github-action/compare/09090944bd8aaa2a517cefb6e38bf1aae336b42b...01e3b659a495b41649cdd0aa82e1d1624e26520b)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: cypress-io/github-action\n  dependency-version: 7.4.4\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: dependencies\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* chore(deps): bump the dependencies group with 13 updates (#8417)\n\nBumps the dependencies group with 13 updates:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [@docsearch/react](https://github.com/algolia/docsearch/tree/HEAD/packages/docsearch-react) | `5.1.0` | `5.1.1` |\n| [react-router](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/tree/HEAD/packages/react-router) | `8.3.1` | `8.4.0` |\n| [tailwind-merge](https://github.com/dcastil/tailwind-merge/tree/HEAD/packages/tailwind-merge) | `3.6.0` | `3.7.0` |\n| [@babel/core](https://github.com/babel/babel/tree/HEAD/packages/babel-core) | `8.0.5` | `8.0.6` |\n| [@babel/preset-env](https://github.com/babel/babel/tree/HEAD/packages/babel-preset-env) | `8.0.5` | `8.0.6` |\n| [@testing-library/dom](https://github.com/testing-library/dom-testing-library) | `10.4.1` | `10.4.2` |\n| [cspell](https://github.com/streetsidesoftware/cspell/tree/HEAD/packages/cspell) | `10.3.1` | `10.3.3` |\n| [eslint-config-webpack](https://github.com/webpack/eslint-config-webpack) | `4.11.0` | `4.14.0` |\n| [jest](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/tree/HEAD/packages/jest) | `30.5.1` | `30.5.2` |\n| [jest-environment-jsdom](https://github.com/jestjs/jest/tree/HEAD/packages/jest-environment-jsdom) | `30.5.1` | `30.5.2` |\n| [prettier](https://github.com/prettier/prettier) | `3.9.6` | `3.9.8` |\n| [webpack](https://github.com/webpack/webpack) | `5.110.3` | `5.111.1` |\n| [webpack-bundle-analyzer](https://github.com/webpack/webpack-bundle-analyzer) | `5.3.3` | `5.4.0` |\n\n\nUpdates `@docsearch/react` from 5.1.0 to 5.1.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/algolia/docsearch/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/algolia/docsearch/blob/main/packages/docsearch-react/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/algolia/docsearch/commits/@docsearch/react@5.1.1/packages/docsearch-react)\n\nUpdates `react-router` from 8.3.1 to 8.4.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/blob/main/packages/react-router/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/commits/react-router@8.4.0/packages/react-router)\n\nUpdates `tailwind-merge` from 3.6.0 to 3.7.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/dcastil/tailwind-merge/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/dcastil/tailwind-merge/commits/tailwind-merge@3.7.0/packages/tailwind-merge)\n\nUpdates `@babel/core` from 8.0.5 to 8.0.6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/babel/babel/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/babel/babel/commits/v8.0.6/packages/babel-core)\n\nUpdates `@babel/preset-env` from 8.0.5 to 8.0.6\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/babel/babel/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/babel/babel/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/babel/babel/commits/v8.0.6/packages/babel-preset-env)\n\nUpdates `@testing-library/dom` from 