e2e runs fail with timeouts.\n\nCopy the frontend files with their directory structure intact and\nremove the stale compressed variants so the freshly assembled\nimportmap and routes registry are the ones served. Same fix as\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2687.","tree":{"sha":"ac47880f83893c208b630e7bb9f77ff029254869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-template-app/git/trees/ac47880f83893c208b630e7bb9f77ff029254869"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-template-app/git/commits/5f4299bd78aaca005c3c69b4816f0ca511392c40","verification":{"payload":"tree ac47880f83893c208b630e7bb9f77ff029254869\nparent 2217adf7e5d42497dc2534ede2a73f473cb0bd90\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1787570888 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787570888 +0530\n\n(chore) Fix the e2e Dockerfile (#343)\n\nThe nightly frontend image now ships precompressed importmap.json and\nroutes.registry.json, and its nginx config serves the .br/.gz variants\nbefore the plain files. The e2e image kept the nightly image''s stale\ncompressed importmap, which points at versioned app directories that\nthe glob COPY flattens, so e2e runs fail with timeouts.\n\nCopy the frontend files with their directory structure intact and\nremove the stale compressed variants so the freshly assembled\nimportmap and routes registry are the ones served. Same fix as\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2687.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjCrICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdUcQAIWCzl+eDl6KbjF1CwlMtVs1\nlGrfroGjjzWBne/mX0HVJym8avdM5zCYP79u1GGrqSqdQMivIFZ/X/S7POuTNWiW\nRGnYfSoAZmbL/vdKjSonuWfuNtUjQF/+rQ0k60k9AiMzlWDO4JKXISgpnND/qtji\nXhYNRLXF8liLhSNJu3uuAAEOaY5G18GYSP3fZfEBbR22OrPiFhpVEFDc7SMp1KSk\nhiV8pJc/iP5K99ClhPBFe9EX89fliUDTH1HFwb+KICVv7Q8TSZUGvQyFQcDzPgvM\nXOyEFJkil1SaZEuiObaQ/nRlWQjIuM2/04QapRO9KH1Pfq8HNTzNYoAdfsbZPh/5\nBLyt0PvloM7CqV6yYRp0kcrSWB3PmKIqj5QpjZxY+zzdSuLfv2yewSAyArn0N8UA\nUeXGWm3Sx7EWrTnk2NCfQHzqQBY8ckbwLdv